### 6.2 Contrast, measured

| Pair | Ratio | Verdict |
|:--|:--|:--|
| Forest text on mint | 13.1 | AAA |
| Forest text on white | 15.3 | AAA |
| Forest text on lime (the lime button) | 11.5 | AAA |
| Lime text on forest | 11.5 | AAA |
| Lime on the inner box `#173A2C` | 9.4 | AAA |
| White text on emerald (the primary button) | 5.2 | AA |
| Emerald text on white | 5.2 | AA |
| Emerald text on mint | 4.4 | large text or UI only |
| `#4E6258` body on white, mint, tint-1 | 6.5, 5.6, 5.9 | AA |
| `#2F4A3D` on the moods card and tint-2 | 7.4, 8.1 | AAA |
| `#B9CDBF` on forest and on the inner box | 9.1, 7.5 | AAA |
| Emerald bar on white, on mint | 5.2, 4.4 | passes the 3:1 non-text rule |
| Lime on white or mint | 1.3 | **fails**: lime never carries text or a bar on a light surface |
| Emerald on forest | 3.0 | borderline: charts on dark cards use the rays, not emerald alone |
| Lime on emerald | 3.9 | UI only, never text |

Rules that follow: lime text only on forest and the inner box; emerald text only at 18 px or larger on mint; the Wilson whiskers are drawn in forest with a white backing so they read over emerald bars (the Codex review's 1.1:1 finding); state colours always pair with an icon and a word.

### 6.3 Typography

- **Bricolage Grotesque** (display): page titles, hero lines, big numbers, the wordmark, mascot name tags. Weights 600 and 800. Sizes 28, 36, 48, 64.
- **Plus Jakarta Sans** (body and UI): everything else. Weights 400, 500, 600, 700. Sizes 13, 14, 16, 18, 22. Body 16 on mobile, 14 to 16 on desktop, line height 1.55.
- **JetBrains Mono** (labels): section eyebrows in uppercase with 0.12 em tracking, hex and ids, timestamps, receipt numbers, counts in tables (tabular figures). Sizes 11, 12, 13.
- Bundled through the Fontsource variable packages for the three faces (verify the exact package names at install), subset to Latin, `font-display: swap`, preloaded only for the two weights above the fold.
- One type scale, one line-height scale, no other faces. The serif Newsreader leaves the product.

### 6.4 Space, shape, depth, motion

- Spacing on a 4-point grid: 4, 8, 12, 16, 24, 32, 48, 64.
- Radius: 8 (chips, inputs), 12 (buttons), 16 (cards), 24 (hero and tool cards, as on the poster).
- Depth by surface, not shadow: mint page, white cards with a `--border` hairline, forest cards for the hero, the header and the tools. Shadows only under mascots and open menus.
- The dot grid on the page background (`--dots`, 2 px dots on a 28 px grid, masked away under dense tables).
- Motion tokens: 120 ms feedback, 200 ms state change, 320 ms enter, 220 ms exit; ease-out in, ease-in out; springs only for mascots. `prefers-reduced-motion` stops every animation, including the demo cursor and the mascot idle.
- Icons: Lucide at 1.75 stroke, 16, 20, 24. No emoji anywhere.

### 6.5 Charts

Emerald single-hue bars on white; the interval printed beside the percentage, never hover-only; the whisker in forest on a white backing; one series per chart, the count on each bar, the axis ending at the denominator; gridlines `--gridline`; a table alternative within a disclosure; chart SVGs scale with a `viewBox` and a responsive width (the 320 px reflow finding). On forest cards, the three rays are the only series colours. The waffle grid is the honest proportion chart for small denominators (10 by 10 cells, each posting a cell, reviewed cells filled).

### 6.6 Components

Refactor in place, in `src/ui/primitives/`: Page, PageHead, SectionLabel, Card (light, tint, forest), Row, Button (primary emerald, lime on forest only, quiet, danger), Tag, Field, Input, Textarea, Select, Spinner, EmptyState, Stat, Kbd, Provenance, BarList. New: `LoopRail`, `SubRail`, `Ring`, `Meter` (the denominator and hours budget), `SkillCard`, `SourcePane`, `ReceiptSlip`, `DecisionCard`, `Mascot`, `MoodBadge`, `Milestone`, `Disclosure`, `Waffle`. Every component has hover, focus-visible, active, disabled and loading states defined in one place, and a 44 px minimum target on touch.

### 6.7 Accessibility baseline

WCAG 2.2 AA as the target: contrast per the table, visible focus everywhere, labels on every control with the visible words in the accessible name, status text beside every colour cue ("Next", "Done"), list and table semantics for chart rows, no hover-only content, 320 px reflow, 200% text zoom, reduced motion, axe in the workspace smoke with zero violations on the loop screens. A screen-reader pass with NVDA on Report before Track B closes.

