## 7. Mascots and living personas

### 7.1 The cast

One shape family, as Duolingo builds Duo and his cast from the same geometry: rounded bodies, big simple eyes with a white catchlight, no mouths beyond a line, detached rounded feet, one prop each tied to the job. Flat, two-tone (a light side top-left, a darker side bottom-right), forest ink outlines at one stroke weight, lime used once per character as the accent, drawn as inline SVG so the same source runs in the app, in Remotion and in the deck.

| Mascot | Job | Body | Prop | Lime accent | How it carries the mood |
|:--|:--|:--|:--|:--|:--|
| Folio | Course reader | A book with a soft spine | A bookmark tab | The tab | Pages open when working; a page curls when waiting |
| Scout | Industry researcher | A rounded explorer with a cap | A small telescope | The lens glint | The telescope sweeps while a fetch runs; lowers when done |
| Atlas | Curriculum mapper | A map-pin shaped body | A thread between two pins | The thread | The thread tightens when a proposal awaits confirmation |
| Lens | Evidence analyst | A magnifier with a handle | A bracket (the interval) | The bracket ends | The bracket narrows as the denominator grows |
| Quill | Course designer | A feather pen | A ruler rail | The nib | The rail blocks (shakes once, no bounce) on a failed check |
| Prism | Teaching-material creator | A triangular prism | The three rays | None (the rays are the ray tokens) | The rays fan out when a pack is generated |
| Steward | Review assistant | A folder with a receipt tab | A clipboard | The receipt tab | Holds the folder out when a brief is ready to send |

The first versions are static SVG with four poses each; they already read as characters. Rigged mouths and Rive state machines are Track B.

### 7.2 Moods, from records only

| Mood | The record that proves it | What the viewer sees |
|:--|:--|:--|
| Resting | Nothing pending for this role on this course | A slow 3 px idle float; nothing else |
| Working | A real request is in flight (a fetch, a scan, a pack render) | The prop moves; a short progress line beside the mascot |
| Waiting for you | A proposal exists and needs confirmation (a scan proposal, a brief awaiting a decision, a check result awaiting adoption) | The mascot faces the control; a lime dot on the rail item |
| Done | The record this step produces was saved in the last few seconds | One spring (damping 12), then rest |
| Stuck | A request failed | No mascot; the error card with the cause, the fix and retry |

A proof suite (`src/prove-moods.ts`) asserts that each mood is a pure function of the workspace state and that no mood is "working" without an in-flight request. The demo clock pins the idle float so recordings are identical.

### 7.3 Placement

Scout beside the fetch control, Atlas beside the proposals, Lens beside the count, Steward beside the brief, Quill in the revision editor, Prism beside the packs, Folio on the course overview. On the rail, each item shows its mascot at 24 px. On How it works, the loop graphic at full size. Never more than one mascot in motion per screen. Never on error, billing or security moments.

### 7.4 Production

- `src/ui/mascots/<name>.tsx`: the SVG as JSX, named groups (`eyes`, `prop`, `arms`), a `mood` prop, a `size` prop, `aria-hidden` with the name in the adjacent label.
- `scripts/gen-mascots.mjs`: renders each mascot at each mood to PNG at 512 and 1024 through Puppeteer into `public/brand/mascots/` for the deck, the brief and the booth banner.
- The Remotion project imports the same components.
- Optional: Gemini images for the landing hero only, in the same palette and style, through the prompts in the archived asset brief rewritten for forest and lime. If they do not match the drawn cast in a side-by-side, they are not used.

