| §9.3, **100 responses, stable at 150; 40 cannot calibrate** | These are overgeneralised. Linacre relates 100 and 150 to specified precision, confidence and targeting conditions, and permits exploratory work with smaller samples; they are not automatic validity thresholds. [Linacre’s table](https://www.rasch.org/rmt/rmt74m.htm). |
| §9.5, **six or more cohorts; one held-out semester** | S §6 requires several observations on each side for interrupted time series, not merely six total. One predictive win does not demonstrate a causal learning gain; Brier scoring also needs a defined probabilistic outcome rather than an unspecified mastery mean. |
| §9.6, **100 to 200 comments** | This is the research note author’s proposed protocol, not an established minimum demonstrated by the cited studies. Label it a planning choice. **S §7.** |
| §11.2, **46 clients** | Supported as a dated showcase count in D §2. It does not verify unchanged operation of Lyceum’s tools, permissions and skill package across every host. |
| §13, **6 to 12 months; $3 to $12; about $22,000; about $14,000** | Procurement duration is vendor guidance; Canvas figures are secondary pricing intelligence. The roughly $14,000 anchor traces to a specific $13,905 Lightcast Analyst renewal in the older pain note §2.2, not general Lightcast/Chmura pricing. **H §4.** |
| §§2.2, 13, **85%; 89%; 30%; more than half** | Preserve survey populations and dates. Tyton’s 89% is willingness to invest, not a spending commitment or demand for Lyceum; identify the consultancy survey source. **H §§4, 6.** |
| §13, **22,000 institutions; 14 million teachers; 45,000 lecturers; billions** | The five notes do not establish these totals. `docs/lyceum-improvement-plan.md` §27 supplies dated UNESCO/MOHE references, institution-definition uncertainty and a much wider spend range; 45,000 approximates 2023 counts, with 2024 verification explicitly outstanding. Adjacent spend is a vendor estimate, not Lyceum’s addressable revenue. |
| §14, **1 of 24 reviewed postings** | Unverified worked example. `public/demo/collected-sample.json` contains ten postings; calculate the displayed numerator and denominator from the actual prepared demonstration state. |
| §14, **TRL 6 and TRL 7** | H §2 supplies an author assessment, not certification or demonstrated fulfilment. One department, one term and LMS integration are proposed milestones, not NASA’s literal requirements. [NASA software criteria](https://esto.nasa.gov/trl/). |
| §16, free below **three video contributors** | V §1 describes employee/organisation and version-dependent licence conditions, including an educational-institution caveat. Contributor count alone does not establish eligibility; free entitlement is unverified. |
| §17.5, **three resets, five-hour bars, 100%, all expiry times** | Account-specific claims unsupported by the research notes and unverified here. They should not determine the critical path. |

The remaining substantive figures are supported at their stated source scope: the event’s date and durations; Singapore’s two-to-five-year review interval; the vendor-labelled 32%, 66% and estimated five-year half-life; US 52%/45%; EU 21.4%; ESCO’s 13,939 skills and 28 languages; and the vendor’s 0-to-100 Skillabi score.

Font sizes, weights, spacing, motion timings, resolutions, encoding settings, pose counts and tool counts are specifications, not research findings. Likewise, interview counts, three-to-five pilot institutions, 50-to-200 lecturers and one-to-two licences are explicitly targets; the four archived pitch documents, nine screenshots and five research notes are present.

## 5. Ten highest-value changes, ranked

1. **Reduce Track A to one reliable evidence-to-teaching walkthrough.** Make every additional package conditional on that path passing on the presentation laptop. **Section 17.1.**

2. **Separate sampling precision, prediction accuracy and causal educational benefit.** Remove the implication that a response threshold establishes representativeness or that beating carry-forward establishes learning gains. **Sections 9.1, 9.5, 9.8.**

3. **Complete the claims register before building public copy or media.** Record population, date, source type and qualification alongside every figure flagged above. **Sections 2, 13, 18.**

4. **Specify a versioned decision contract with permissions, persistence and backup validation.** Connect the decision to its brief and revision, including valid keep, defer and return paths. **Sections 4, 8.**

5. **Move new Learn analytics out of Amsterdam scope.** Demonstrate existing imports only with explicitly illustrative, matched course and term data. **Sections 9, 15, 17.2.**

6. **Protect source inspection ahead of decorative visual work.** Put the quotation in context and distinguish literal matching from correct interpretation of a requirement. **Sections 5.3, 17.1.**

7. **Timebox one local evidence-report MCP tool after the core is stable.** Demonstrate a fresh dated export and label remote tenant integration planned. **Sections 11.4, 17.1.**

8. **Replace unconditional TRL 6 wording with a documented self-assessment.** State the demonstrated environment, current limitations and evidence needed for the next readiness claim. **Sections 1, 14.**

9. **Add a price hypothesis and a specific department pilot offer.** Define the buyer, existing-process baseline, success measures and conversion decision without treating general AI interest as demand. **Sections 13, 14.**

10. **Use native PowerPoint and one captioned product recording.** Rehearse the exact submitted files, offline fallback and booth reset process before freeze. **Sections 14 to 17.**

## 6. Design, Sections 6 to 8

- **The visual system risks looking assembled from fashionable references.** Forest cards, electric lime, dot grids, uppercase monospace labels, large rounded containers and seven mascots are collectively busy. Keep the approved palette, but make white evidence surfaces, restrained headings and document-like layouts dominant. **Sections 6.3 to 6.6.**

- **Seven large-eyed characters can infantilise an academic review task.** Put restrained static illustrations on onboarding and How it works; use ordinary labelled icons in navigation and evidence work. Avoid speaking avatars and repeated character celebrations until lecturer testing supports them. **Sections 7.1, 7.3, 8; V §§2, 3.**

- **The ring suggests that adoption is always desirable.** Use a labelled progress list with “review complete, no change needed,” deferred and stale states; show provenance rather than rewarding every saved action. **Sections 4, 8.**

- **The waffle specification is mathematically ambiguous.** A 10-by-10 grid cannot simultaneously mean one posting per cell and an honest proportion for arbitrary denominators. Use exactly N marks for small sets or a labelled proportion bar, keeping review completeness separate from skill prevalence. **Section 6.5.**

- **Contrast needs functional tokens, not just brand pairings.** Emerald on forest fails 3:1, including `ray-1`; the pale border is only about 1.36:1 on white and cannot be the sole identifying boundary of an input. Add explicit control and focus tokens, and use forest for small text on mint. **Sections 6.1, 6.2, 6.6; [W3C non-text contrast](https://www.w3.org/WAI/WCAG22/Understanding/non-text-contrast.html).**

- **Small labels and miniature mascots weaken legibility.** Reserve 11-to-13 px tracked monospace for genuinely secondary metadata, keep essential labels comfortably readable, and simplify illustrations at navigation size. Source dates, denominators and uncertainty must remain visible. **Sections 6.3, 7.3.**

- **Cards can make comparison harder.** Preserve a compact accessible table alongside skill summaries, and keep quotation context beside confirmation controls; “one primary action” should not hide necessary evidence. **Sections 5.3, 6.5, 6.6.**

- **Automated checks do not cover the proposed interaction changes.** Before freeze, test keyboard tabs, route focus, disclosures, error announcements, zoom, narrow layouts and reduced motion, plus a screen-reader pass through Report and Decide. Keep WCAG AA labelled as a target until the broader audit is complete. **Sections 6.7, 17.1, 17.2.**
