## 1. Sceptical judge assessment

I read all requested files and made no changes. Section references below refer to [docs/lyceum-upgrade-plan.md](<C:/Users/abdul/OneDrive/Documents/01 Coding Project/27 Lyceum V3/docs/lyceum-upgrade-plan.md>); runtime behaviour, historical test passes and unpublished organiser materials remain unverified.

| Criterion | Assessment |
|:--|:--|
| Innovation, 30% | **Overclaim:** competitor marketing pages cannot establish that “none” offers these capabilities, and seven named roles do not establish an agentic architecture. **Underclaim:** quotation validation, explicit denominators and reproducible exports are tangible differentiation. Judge question: “What does the AI actually do, and what does Lyceum enforce that an assistant alone cannot?” **Sections 1, 11, 13, 14.** |
| Technology Readiness, 20% | **Overclaim:** TRL 6 is asserted without documenting a full-scale realistic lecturer problem, relevant environment or deployment evidence. Automated checks support software correctness, not institutional readiness; the local export adapter also does not prove university integration. Judge question: “Who outside the team has completed this workflow?” **Sections 1, 11.4, 14.** |
| Commercial Viability, 15% | **Overclaim:** free local use does not remove installation, review labour, procurement or integration costs, and deterministic calculations do not establish near-zero service costs. Missing: an actual price hypothesis, named initial buyer, support assumptions and a reason to pay when the free tier includes the whole loop and exports. **Sections 3, 13.** |
| Education Significance, 15% | **Overclaim:** underemployment statistics do not establish curriculum latency as their cause; better prediction does not establish learning improvement. **Underclaim:** preserving foundational content and tracing evidence into an outcome, activity and assessment is demonstrable educational value. Judge question: “Which review task improves, compared with the lecturer’s existing process?” **Sections 2.1, 4, 9.5, 9.8, 14.** |
| Presentation, 10% | The receipt opening is strong, but eleven slides, seven characters, a dense architecture diagram, several application switches and statistical terminology compete for eight minutes. The proposed latency graphic also juxtaposes months and percentages without a meaningful common scale. Keep the story on one course decision and move detailed architecture to questions. **Sections 12, 14, 16.** |
| Demo, 10% | The rejection of an invalid quotation and editable pack are convincing. However, role switching is a local persona simulation, filing sample results does not close a real semester, and the assistant reads an exported snapshot rather than the live workspace. State those boundaries during the demonstration. **Sections 4, 11.4, 15.** |

## 2. Contradictions and gaps inside the plan and against current code

- **The new flow is a substantial migration.** [src/app/journey.ts](<C:/Users/abdul/OneDrive/Documents/01 Coding Project/27 Lyceum V3/src/app/journey.ts>) currently orders outline adoption before evidence and finishes at brief preparation. `src/App.tsx` recognises flat screen hashes, while `navigate()` takes only a screen; the proposed course routes require routing, permission, back-navigation and unsaved-edit work beyond shell restyling. **Sections 4, 5.2, 17.1.**

- **Decide needs more than a record and three buttons.** There is no `BriefDecision` in `src/types.ts`, persistence or backup validation. Specify permitted actors, conflicting decisions, superseded briefs, links to the proposed revision, and restoration of older backups; A2a omits explicit changes to `src/lib/workspaceBackup.ts`. **Sections 4, 11.3, 17.4.**

- **The ring can reward unnecessary changes.** Update completes only after adoption, although a defensible decision can retain the course, defer action or return the brief. Completion also needs term and version scope, invalidation rules and a legitimate “no change required” path; otherwise old records can complete a new semester. **Sections 3, 4, 8.**

- **Learn is simultaneously promised and deferred.** A2b and the booth require attainment, survey comparisons and sample adequacy, while B2 owns their implementation. `ResultUpload` stores aggregated means, standard deviations and counts, without the taught version or cohort population; it cannot supply respondent-level bias comparisons or student bootstrap resampling. **Sections 4, 9, 15, 17.1, 17.2.**

- **The supplied Learn samples do not match.** `scripts/gen-demo-files.mjs` generates CS310 results for 2025-S1 and a CS220/CLO4 survey for 2025-S1, whereas [src/demo/script.ts](<C:/Users/abdul/OneDrive/Documents/01 Coding Project/27 Lyceum V3/src/demo/script.ts>) edits CS310 for 2026/2027. These cannot establish the proposed perception comparison or results matched to the taught version. **Sections 4, 9.4, 15.**

- **The timeline is not an immutable audit trail.** [src/app/runs.ts](<C:/Users/abdul/OneDrive/Documents/01 Coding Project/27 Lyceum V3/src/app/runs.ts>) timestamps the current count using source `addedAt`, not review time, and reports teaching packs as available rather than downloaded. Download milestones and historical evidence states need additional records. **Sections 8, 12, 18.**

- **Current product copy contradicts current behaviour.** [src/ui/screens/EvidenceWorkspace.tsx](<C:/Users/abdul/OneDrive/Documents/01 Coding Project/27 Lyceum V3/src/ui/screens/EvidenceWorkspace.tsx>) says nothing is collected from the web immediately above `ResearchRun`. [README.md](<C:/Users/abdul/OneDrive/Documents/01 Coding Project/27 Lyceum V3/README.md>) describes a saved-sample tour, but the script attempts live collection first and falls back only on failure, undermining repeatable capture. **Sections 0, 15, 16, 18.**

- **The theme migration needs compatibility rules.** [src/theme/tokens.ts](<C:/Users/abdul/OneDrive/Documents/01 Coding Project/27 Lyceum V3/src/theme/tokens.ts>) and existing components use names such as `accent`, `surface`, `ok` and `controlBorder`, absent from the proposed token table. Preserve aliases or explicitly migrate consumers; also remove the runtime Google Fonts links in `index.html`. **Sections 6.1, 6.3, 17.4.**

- **The local door has unresolved semantics.** “Writes nothing” contradicts the PPTX-producing tool; say “does not mutate workspace records.” The booth needs an explicit export-refresh step, and remote private reads need authentication even when tools are read-only. **Sections 11.2 to 11.4, 15.**

- **Several binding rules conflict.** Idle floating contradicts motion only during requests or record changes; Quill shakes on failed checks despite the error prohibition; B7 contradicts the unconditional ban on model-written artefacts; the video introduces a gradient and an undeclared hex value. Optional production Gemini artwork also conflicts with [DECISIONS.md](<C:/Users/abdul/OneDrive/Documents/01 Coding Project/27 Lyceum V3/DECISIONS.md>)’s 22 October decision that generated images are concept art only. **Sections 0, 6, 7, 16, 17.2.**

- **The delivery format is unresolved.** PowerPoint and video are the stated media, but the presentation depends on HTML. An image-per-slide PPTX does not preserve the HTML film, interactions or accessible text; acceptance must cover the actual submitted presentation. **Sections 14.3, 17.1.**

## 3. Track A schedule

**Every weekday in Section 17.1 is wrong for 2026:** 23 October is Friday, 24 Saturday, 25 Sunday, 26 Monday and 27 Tuesday. Resolve whether freeze means Monday 26 or Tuesday 27 at noon, with a timezone and confirmed travel deadline.

A2a and A2b are not independent parallel sessions: they share navigation, journey state, Home and the data model. A6 and A7 also require developer work on generators and capture infrastructure, despite being assigned separate team lanes. Seven teammates can own copy, slides, voice, claims and testing, but that does not create additional implementation or integration capacity. **Sections 17.1, 17.3.**

The 30-minute branch review is a triage budget, not evidence that snapshots are safe to integrate. Passing existing proofs does not establish comparable collection windows or compatibility with the new flow. **Section 17.1, A0.**

Cut in this order:

1. **The second film, speaking avatars and bespoke deck generator.** Keep one captioned product recording and a native PowerPoint deck; protect content and playback rather than production infrastructure. **A6, A7.**
2. **Animated mascot poses, the waffle and repeated rings.** Retain static identity and clear navigation; preserve the source pane because source inspection demonstrates the central promise. **A1, A2a, A3.**
3. **New Learn analytics and wholesale route replacement.** Mark Learn as future work and align visible labels around the existing reliable workflow. **A2b, B2.**
4. **Five of the six MCP tools.** Timebox one evidence-report tool after the core passes; drop it if unreliable, but do not sacrifice it before decorative work while promising a platform answer. **A5.**

A more credible four-day sequence:

| Date | Developer and agent | Teammates |
|:--|:--|:--|
| Friday 23 | Establish recoverable baseline, triage branch, fix misleading copy, freeze scope and sample | Claims register, buyer questions, talk track |
| Saturday 24 | Source inspection and minimal persisted decision flow, including restore and stale-state checks | Native deck, brief, poster |
| Sunday 25 | Stabilise demo; optional single MCP tool after checks pass | Independent walkthroughs, captioned capture, accessibility checks |
| Monday 26 | Fix defects and rehearse on the actual laptop | Test submitted files, offline fallbacks, printing and packing |

Missing from the day plan: claims before screen and media production; a purpose-built starting backup rather than the demo’s completed state; matched demonstration fixtures; empty-live-result recovery; backup migration checks; fresh MCP exports; and a protected repair buffer. The current script estimates **336.68 seconds**, about **5:37**, including introductions, so a six-minute path with extra decision, Learn, PowerPoint and assistant interactions needs a substantially shorter script. **Sections 15, 17.1; `src/demo/script.ts`.**

